__pycache__/
*.pyc
.store/

# The two token files. A token in a repository is not a token; write your own:
#   echo '{"dev-reader": "*"}'                   > server/readers.json
#   echo '["<account-uuid>.<secret>"]'            > server/tokens.json
readers.json
tokens.json

# The staged FreeBSD package trees: hundreds of MB of somebody else's binaries,
# one per component, rebuilt by `server/oci/stage-freebsd.sh` in seconds and
# never a source of truth.
oci/stage-freebsd*/
oci/rootfs*
oci/*.version
oci/*.manifest

# The compose stack's per-operator settings: the domain, the TLS directory and
# the paths to the two token files. `compose.yml` tells you to write it, so it
# is a file that WILL exist on every deployment -- and it names a host's real
# certificate directory and can point at the token files themselves. Committing
# one publishes another machine's layout and makes `docker compose up` in a
# fresh checkout read somebody else's paths. `oci/.env.example` is the copy
# that IS tracked.
oci/.env
